  "interpretation": [
    "The distribution of all evaluated checkpoints is centered on the paired BC baseline (collision mean 20.72 vs BC 21; overtake mean 344.4 vs BC 346). Across seven stages that varied hard-pool content, sampling mode, hard probability, batch size, rollout cadence, LR x target-KL, exploration std, and their transfer/interaction, the distribution did not move.",
    "The best observed value (15 collisions, V1.1 U2 / AH-H0-p50-wr U2) sits at the expected minimum of ~46 draws from the same noise distribution (14.5). Under collision-first minimum selection this is the outcome expected when no arm has any real effect (winner's curse).",
    "Paired churn is symmetric (mean fixed 6.96 vs mean new 6.67 per checkpoint, n=46): updates flip marginal scenarios in both directions rather than systematically removing collisions.",
    "Caveat: the 46 checkpoints are not fully independent (shared parent arms, U2/U4 within runs). Positive dependence reduces the effective n, which raises the expected minimum toward the observed 15; the iid calculation is therefore not overstating the case."
  ],
  "binding_conclusion": "No configuration in the reduced 22-arm study produced a detectable improvement over paired BC on the development panel. The development-panel numbers of these 46 checkpoints are exhausted as evidence: no further checkpoint selection, ranking, or best-of claims may be made from them. Any future improvement claim requires a pre-registered test on a panel that was not used for selection.",
